    "Scouting Notes": "Stands out for his defensive skill set. Though a lack of focus may have caused a high number of passed balls. The skillset is really impressive.\n Flexible and agile behind the plate.\n Said to be a high energy player who works well with pitchers.\n Strong throwing arm and has thrown out 35% of attempted base stealers in his career thus far.\n Has shown huge raw power, hitting a 110 MPH HR in the ACL in 2022, as well as an ability to elevate the ball regularly.\n Shows a willingness to take walks, but also strikes out a lot.\n Will need to improve the bat to ball skills and hit tool to be worthy of much attention, but the defense and raw power gives a base worth keeping an eye on.\n Catchers are hard to find, so if he shows improvement in the areas above, he could be a big mover. Otherwise he's probably org depth.",
